{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that translates C++ code to Java 8 code. The code should reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Translate the following GNU C++17 code to Java 8 code. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your translated code should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input.\nPrint your translated code and also the confidence score you give to your translation. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<translated_code>\n<your_translated_code>\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the original GNU C++17 code you have to translate:\n<original_code>\n#include <iostream>\n#include <algorithm>\n#include <functional>\n#include <map>\n#include <queue>\n#include <tuple>\n#include <vector>\nusing namespace std;\nusing ll = long long;\n\nconst ll INF = 100000000LL;\nconst ll BIG = (1LL << 62);\nll A[20];\n\nint main() {\n    ios::sync_with_stdio(false);\n    cin.tie(nullptr);\n\n    ll n;\n    cin >> n;\n\n    for (int i = 1; i <= 16; ++i)\n        A[i] = A[i - 1] * 10 + 1;\n\n    if (n < 0) n = -n;\n\n    map<pair<int, ll>, ll> dist;\n    priority_queue<tuple<ll, int, ll>, vector<tuple<ll, int, ll>>, greater<tuple<ll, int, ll>>> pq;\n\n    dist[{16, n}] = 0;\n    pq.push({0, 16, n});\n\n    auto relax = [&](int ni, ll nv, ll nd) {\n        if (ni > 0 && nv < 0) nv = -nv;\n        auto key = make_pair(ni, nv);\n        auto it = dist.find(key);\n        if (it == dist.end() || nd < it->second) {\n            dist[key] = nd;\n            pq.push({nd, ni, nv});\n        }\n    };\n\n    ll answer = BIG;\n\n    while (!pq.empty()) {\n        auto [d, idx, val] = pq.top();\n        pq.pop();\n\n        auto key = make_pair(idx, val);\n        auto it = dist.find(key);\n        if (it == dist.end() || it->second != d) continue;\n\n        if (idx == 0) {\n            ll total = d + (val == 0 ? 0 : INF);\n            if (total < answer) answer = total;\n            continue;\n        }\n\n        ll q = val / A[idx];\n        relax(idx - 1, val - q * A[idx], d + q * idx);\n        relax(idx - 1, val - (q + 1) * A[idx], d + (q + 1) * idx);\n    }\n\n    cout << answer << '\\n';\n    return 0;\n}\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<translated_code>\nimport java.util.*;\n\npublic class Main {\n    static final long INF = 100000000L;\n    static final long BIG = 1L << 62;\n    static long[] A = new long[20];\n\n    static class Key {\n        int idx;\n        long val;\n        Key(int i, long v) { idx = i; val = v; }\n        @Override\n        public boolean equals(Object o) {\n            if (this == o) return true;\n            if (!(o instanceof Key)) return false;\n            Key k = (Key) o;\n            return idx == k.idx && val == k.val;\n        }\n        @Override\n        public int hashCode() {\n            return 31 * idx + (int)(val ^ (val >>> 32));\n        }\n    }\n\n    static class Node implements Comparable<Node> {\n        long dist;\n        int idx;\n        long val;\n        Node(long d, int i, long v) { dist = d; idx = i; val = v; }\n        @Override\n        public int compareTo(Node other) {\n            return Long.compare(this.dist, other.dist);\n        }\n    }\n\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);\n        long n = sc.nextLong();\n        sc.close();\n\n        // Initialize A\n        A[0] = 0;\n        for (int i = 1; i <= 16; ++i) {\n            A[i] = A[i-1] * 10 + 1;\n        }\n\n        if (n < 0) n = -n;\n\n        Map<Key, Long> dist = new HashMap<>();\n        PriorityQueue<Node> pq = new PriorityQueue<>();\n\n        dist.put(new Key(16, n), 0L);\n        pq.add(new Node(0, 16, n));\n\n        long answer = BIG;\n\n        while (!pq.isEmpty()) {\n            Node cur = pq.poll();\n            long d = cur.dist;\n            int idx = cur.idx;\n            long val = cur.val;\n\n            Key key = new Key(idx, val);\n            Long stored = dist.get(key);\n            if (stored == null || stored != d) continue;\n\n            if (idx == 0) {\n                long total = d + (val == 0 ? 0 : INF);\n                if (total < answer) answer = total;\n                continue;\n            }\n\n            long q = val / A[idx];\n            // relax with q\n            {\n                int ni = idx - 1;\n                long nv = val - q * A[idx];\n                long nd = d + q * idx;\n                if (ni > 0 && nv < 0) nv = -nv;\n                Key nkey = new Key(ni, nv);\n                Long old = dist.get(nkey);\n                if (old == null || nd < old) {\n                    dist.put(nkey, nd);\n                    pq.add(new Node(nd, ni, nv));\n                }\n            }\n            // relax with q+1\n            {\n                int ni = idx - 1;\n                long nv = val - (q + 1) * A[idx];\n                long nd = d + (q + 1) * idx;\n                if (ni > 0 && nv < 0) nv = -nv;\n                Key nkey = new Key(ni, nv);\n                Long old = dist.get(nkey);\n                if (old == null || nd < old) {\n                    dist.put(nkey, nd);\n                    pq.add(new Node(nd, ni, nv));\n                }\n            }\n        }\n\n        System.out.println(answer);\n    }\n}\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n0.95\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [-7.271740287251305e-06, -0.320160835981369, -1.7881233361549675e-05, -1.1920928244535389e-07, 0.0, -0.0001691436773398891, -0.00028534632292576134, 0.0, -9.619726915843785e-05, -0.0015718498034402728, -0.0004371640970930457, 0.0, -2.3841830625315197e-06